@startuml UC-101: Register Sample & Verify Suitability
title UC-101: Register Sample & Verify Suitability\nActor: Reception Technician

start

:Select correct request ID;
:Select sampling location and precise GPS Sampling Point;
:Input sample type, collection time, collector ID,\ncontainer type, receipt temperature, and volume;

' Fixing Deadlock: AF-2 modeled sequentially to ensure reliable token flow
if (Operator requests split sample? [AF-2]) then (yes)
  :Create sub-sample record;
  :Copy original ID to parent reference field;
  if (Test is external?) then (yes)
    :Set external referral flag to true;
    :Record external laboratory ID;
  else (no)
  endif
else (no)
endif

:System generates unique laboratory reference ID;
:System evaluates sample metrics against suitability matrix rules;

if (Critical defect found?\n(Leak, Expired Time, or Wrong Container) [EF-1]) then (yes)
  :Set status to "Rejected";
  :Lock sample record;
  :Notification subsystem sends alert to contact list within 5 minutes;
  stop

elseif (Metrics pass basic rules?) then (yes)
  :Set status to "Accepted";

else (Data Incomplete or Near Thresholds [AF-1])
  :Prompt user for receipt condition notes;
  :Input specific defects of the data;
  :Set status to "Provisionally Accepted";
  :Start 48-hour data rejection countdown timer;
endif

' Fixing Implicit Merge: Unified Merge Diamond before Step 7 Action Node
if (Merge alternative workflows) then
  ' Internal routing from Accepted or Provisionally Accepted branches
endif

:Create first row in Chain of Custody log\n(Location set to "Reception");
:Show confirmation message to user;

stop
@enduml
